; The root zone of the lab's internet. A line is a record: a name, a TTL
; (or the $TTL below), IN, the type and the value. A name without a final
; dot has the zone's name added to it.
$TTL 86400
.                    IN SOA a.root-servers.test. hostmaster.nic.test. ( 2026111201 1800 900 604800 86400 ) ; serial
.                    IN NS  a.root-servers.test.
a.root-servers.test. IN A   198.51.100.11
; test. is delegated to its own server, with glue (the server's address)
test.                IN NS  ns1.nic.test.
ns1.nic.test.        IN A   198.51.100.12
; test.'s DS record, the hash of its key, is added below when the lab is built
